1
00:02:58,064 --> 00:03:04,064
The toys are back!

2
00:05:56,129 --> 00:06:02,129
Toy Story 2 is a animation, comedy, family film directed by John Lasseter.

3
00:08:54,193 --> 00:09:00,193
Andy heads off to Cowboy Camp, leaving his toys to their own devices.

4
00:11:52,258 --> 00:11:58,258
Things shift into high gear when an obsessive toy collector named
Al McWhiggen, owner of Al's Toy Barn kidnaps Woody.

5
00:14:50,322 --> 00:14:56,322
Andy's toys mount a daring rescue mission, Buzz Lightyear meets his match
and Woody has to decide where he and his heart truly belong.

6
00:17:48,387 --> 00:17:54,387
Woody (voice), played by Tom Hanks.

7
00:20:46,451 --> 00:20:52,451
Buzz Lightyear (voice), played by Tim Allen.

8
00:23:44,516 --> 00:23:50,516
Jessie (voice), played by Joan Cusack.

9
00:26:42,580 --> 00:26:48,580
Prospector (voice), played by Kelsey Grammer.

10
00:29:40,645 --> 00:29:46,645
Mr. Potato Head (voice), played by Don Rickles.

11
00:32:38,709 --> 00:32:44,709
Slinky Dog (voice), played by Jim Varney.

12
00:35:36,774 --> 00:35:42,774
Toy Story 2 is a 1999 American animated adventure comedy-drama film
produced by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures.

13
00:38:34,838 --> 00:38:40,838
It is the second installment in Pixar's Toy Story franchise
and the sequel to the original 1995 film.

14
00:41:32,903 --> 00:41:38,903
The film was directed by John Lasseter from a screenplay by Andrew
Stanton, Rita Hsiao, Doug Chamberlin, and Chris Webb.

15
00:44:30,967 --> 00:44:36,967
Tom Hanks, Tim Allen, Don Rickles, Jim Varney, Wallace
Shawn, John Ratzenberger, Annie Potts, R.

16
00:47:29,032 --> 00:47:35,032
Lee Ermey, John Morris, Laurie Metcalf and Jeff Pidgeon reprise their roles from the first Toy Story  film, with
newcomers Joan Cusack, Kelsey Grammer, Wayne Knight, Estelle Harris, and Jodi Benson joining the cast.

17
00:50:27,096 --> 00:50:33,096
In the film, Woody is stolen by a greedy toy collector, prompting Buzz Lightyear and his friends
to save him, but Woody is then tempted by the idea of immortality in a museum.

18
00:53:25,161 --> 00:53:31,161
Disney initially envisioned Toy Story 2 as a direct-to-video sequel.

19
00:56:23,225 --> 00:56:29,225
The film began production in a building separated from Pixar, on a small scale, as
most of the main Pixar staff were busy working on A Bug's Life (1998).

20
00:59:21,290 --> 00:59:27,290
When story reels proved promising, Disney upgraded the film to a
theatrical release, but Pixar was unhappy with the film's quality.

21
01:02:19,354 --> 01:02:25,354
Lasseter and the story team redeveloped the entire plot in one weekend.

22
01:05:17,419 --> 01:05:23,419
Although most Pixar features take years to develop, the established release date could not be
moved and the production schedule for Toy Story 2 was compressed into nine months.

23
01:08:15,483 --> 01:08:21,483
Despite production struggles, Toy Story 2 premiered at the El Capitan Theatre on November 13, 1999, and was
released on November 24 to box office success, grossing $511 million against a $90 million budget.

24
01:11:13,548 --> 01:11:19,548
It received widespread acclaim from critics, with a 100% rating on the
website Rotten Tomatoes, similar to its predecessor.

25
01:14:11,612 --> 01:14:17,612
It is considered by critics to be one of the few sequel films superior to the original and
is frequently featured on lists of the greatest animated films ever made.

26
01:17:09,677 --> 01:17:15,677
Toy Story 2 would go on to become the third-highest-grossing film of 1999.

27
01:20:07,741 --> 01:20:13,741
Among its accolades, the film won Best Motion Picture –
Musical or Comedy at the 57th Golden Globe Awards.

28
01:23:05,806 --> 01:23:11,806
A sequel, Toy Story 3, was released in 2010.

29
01:26:03,870 --> 01:26:09,870
The film explores themes of friendship, airplane,
museum, prosecution, identity crisis.

30
01:29:01,935 --> 01:29:07,935
The tone is lighthearted.
